WEBVTT

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.398
looking and finding shapes in the clouds

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:31.741
when they were kids?

00:01:31.765 --> 00:01:38.472
You know, when you were
masters of daydreaming?

00:01:38.496 --> 00:01:41.239
Aristophanes, the ancient
Greek playwright,

00:01:41.263 --> 00:01:44.590
he described the clouds
as the patron godesses

00:01:44.614 --> 00:01:46.374
of idle fellows

00:01:46.398 --> 00:01:48.018
two and a half thousand years ago,

00:01:48.042 --> 00:01:49.471
and you can see what he means.

00:01:49.495 --> 00:01:53.928
It's just that these days,
us adults seem reluctant

00:01:53.952 --> 00:01:57.288
to allow ourselves the indulgence

00:01:57.312 --> 00:01:59.920
of just allowing our imaginations

00:01:59.944 --> 00:02:03.590
to drift along in the breeze,
and I think that's a pity.